      "id": "4e7e17ee-61e4-4dd7-a4a9-ec07eccd30b3",
      "name": "ldaps",
      "description": {
        "content": "Lightweight Directory Access Protocol (LDAP)-based directory servers may store and provide POSIX user and group attributes, as used by the NFS client access protocol. Up to two LDAP configurations are supported, where one is used for binding to the LDAP domain of an Active Directory server and the other is used for connecting to a different LDAP-based server other than AD. Limitations apply to the combinations of external providers and protocol enablement.",
        "type": "text/plain"
      },
